---
import MarketingLayout from "../layouts/MarketingLayout.astro";
import { SITE } from "../data/site";
---

<MarketingLayout
  title="Privacy"
  description="Cavren's privacy policy: your data stays on your device. No servers, no harvesting."
  ogType="article"
  canonical={`${SITE.url}/privacy`}
>
  <section class="page">
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Short version: Cavren is a community, local-first tool. Your resumes stay on
      your device. We don't run an app server for your content, we don't require
      accounts, and we don't embed analytics or advertising trackers.
    </p>

    <div class="prose">
      <h2>Where your data lives</h2>
      <p>
        Resumes are stored in this browser's IndexedDB. Backups you download
        (.r.json, PDF, DOCX) are ordinary files on your computer. Optional
        version snapshots also stay in IndexedDB on this device.
      </p>

      <h2>What we collect</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>No account, no name, no email required to build or export.</li>
        <li>No analytics, advertising, or session-replay scripts.</li>
        <li>
          Hosted fonts ship with the app — we do not load third-party tracking
          domains.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Optional AI</h2>
      <p>
        AI features are off until you configure them. You can use on-device
        Chrome AI or supply your own API key. Text you explicitly send goes only
        to that provider — never to a Cavren-hosted model. You can clear the key
        anytime in AI settings.
      </p>

      <h2>Optional Google Drive backup</h2>
      <p>
        If you enable Drive backup, OAuth runs in your browser against Google.
        The backup file is written to <em>your</em> Drive. Cavren does not
        operate a sync server. Tokens stay in this browser.
      </p>

      <h2>Exports &amp; offline</h2>
      <p>
        PDF and DOCX are generated locally. Once installed as a PWA (or after a
        visit), the app shell can work offline for editing and export. Network is
        only needed for optional AI APIs and Drive.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions? Reach us at{" "}
        <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a> or visit{" "}
        <a href="/contact">contact</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</MarketingLayout>
